# BUG-247 regression fixture — a non-ASCII byte must NOT be reported as a character.
#
# The identifier below is `café`. Zebra identifiers are ASCII-only, so this is correctly
# REJECTED — that part was never the bug and there is no silent corruption here.
#
# The bug was the MESSAGE. `lexErr` receives `src[pos]`, a raw byte typed `char` (BUG-225),
# and rendered it with `.toString()` — widening lead byte 0xC3 to U+00C3 and reporting
#     unexpected character 'Ã'
# for a source file containing no `Ã`. The column was right; the character was fiction, and
# it sends a reader looking for a character they never typed.
#
# Registered with smoke_run_fail, which also asserts no `.zig:` path leaks into the
# diagnostic — this must stay a Zebra error, not a Zig one.
def main()
    var café = 1
    print(café.toString())
